    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0045_d2c63e98ae55.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:1.82708in;height:1.42014in\" /></p><p>Let, the third vertex be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Area of triangle,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>a</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>a</mi></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;</p><p>i.e. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;or <math><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></math><br /><br />Hence, the sum of the square of the possible values of abscissa <math><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn></math></p>"
  }
